# Line endings are load-bearing in this repository, so they are pinned rather than left to
# each developer's core.autocrlf.
#
# The vendored copy of this package in the consumer repositories is verified by a tree hash
# over file BYTES. With autocrlf=true, git rewrites checked-out files to CRLF, which changes
# those bytes and makes the gate fail on Windows while passing on Linux CI — a false
# positive that trains people to ignore a real drift check.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Fixture bytes ARE the contract: their digests are asserted, and the generator must
# reproduce them byte for byte.
*.jsonl -text
*.zip binary
validation-datasets/adversarial/expected-codes.json -text
